item.text:
{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Tier-1 member owning bounded steps, transitions, intake, execution units, admission, applicability, output, configurations, roles, context construction and fit, acquisition, activation, evaluation, derived-surface staleness, result refinements, disposition, totality, refinement, licensing, work state, restart, cost, proportionality, closed results and reuse. It uses rather than redefines the objects, core algebra and frame activation outcomes owned by FOUNDATIONS and REFERENCE_FRAME. Its rc.2 RF routes are provenance only.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":28,
          "quote":"core for admission, activation and steps (§3); it redefines nothing those\nmembers own. A route\nwritten `rc.2 RF #anchor` is into\n`stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md` and is\nprovenance only.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION",
          "start_line":24
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_member",
      "label":"ACTIVATION"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Activation of one reference frame or one declared active frame configuration on an exact subject. Intake, admission, applicability and activation remain distinct relations even within one invocation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":37,
          "quote":"A step is the activation of one reference frame, or one declared active\nframe configuration, on an exact subject (REFERENCE_FRAME §1, §11). Its\ncontext is the projection of that activated frame to the actor; the corpus\nor the workspace is never the context (P0; RF-002). Intake, admission,\napplicability and activation are distinct relations inside the step even\nwhen one invocation performs all of them.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step",
          "start_line":32
        }
      ],
      "key":"step",
      "label":"Step"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The projection of an activated frame to its actor, providing an account of current state. It is neither the corpus, the workspace nor the state itself.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":35,
          "quote":"context is the projection of that activated frame to the actor; the corpus\nor the workspace is never the context",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step",
          "start_line":34
        },
        {
          "end_line":124,
          "quote":"An actor's context is an account of the\ncurrent state, not the state itself",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":123
        }
      ],
      "key":"actor_context",
      "label":"Actor context"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The material workspace and its authoritative inputs, together with justifiable knowledge and explicit unknowns. Its account includes relevant external observations acquired through their owning interfaces and can be incomplete or stale; the workspace remains the subject. Construction denotes this state by A.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":123,
          "quote":"The current state is the material state of the workspace and\nits authoritative inputs, together with what is justifiably known about\nthat state, with the unknowns explicit.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":118
        },
        {
          "end_line":216,
          "quote":"an actor's\nacquired account can be incomplete or stale, and the workspace, not the\naccount, is the subject",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":214
        }
      ],
      "key":"current_state",
      "label":"Current state A"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"An owner-defined predicate over realised states: the selected outcome, its acceptance conditions and governing obligations. Several states may satisfy it. Construction denotes it by Z; the governing specification, comprising the selected WHAT across Intent, Product and Specification, supplies it and descriptions refine it.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":131,
          "quote":"The destination is defined by constraints: the selected outcome with its\nacceptance conditions (Outcome U, [FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#2-ontology))\nand the governing obligations the work must keep. It names no single\nstate: its acceptance conditions admit several realised states. Its\nowning authority defines it (P2, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":127
        },
        {
          "end_line":219,
          "quote":"The\ngoverning specification, the selected WHAT across the Intent, Product and\nSpecification of the Product that owns the work, supplies Z; its\ndescriptions refine Z.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":216
        }
      ],
      "key":"destination",
      "label":"Destination Z"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A bounded change from current state to next state, carried out by one step. Work exceeding one activation is refined into a series of such transitions; work fitting one activation is one transition. Each binds the applicable outer obligations of the destination and affected governing relations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":140,
          "quote":"A transition is a bounded change from the current state to a next state,\ncarried out by one step. Where the work exceeds one activation's capacity,\nthe outer transformation towards the destination is refined into a series\nof bounded transitions under §4 Refinement, each carried out by its own\nstep; work that fits one activation is a single transition.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":133
        }
      ],
      "key":"transition",
      "label":"Transition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The corpus-owned relation binding A and Z, selecting work and strategy, composing steps, using feedback and claiming completion. Its subject accounts are distinct: specification states required conditions; observations state what holds; a causal or predictive model explains possible state changes. A composition boundary connects one step's output to the next starting state and differs from a categorical join between categories. Feedback observes, compares, diagnoses, selects an authorised response, acts and observes again. Homeostasis is correction toward requirements, without guaranteed convergence or requirement adequacy.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":207,
          "quote":"This subsection states the construction relation for this corpus: how a\nselected construction binds its current state and destination, chooses\nits work, composes its steps, corrects itself and claims completion.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":200
        },
        {
          "end_line":237,
          "quote":"The specification is the internal reference model of the required\nconditions. Observations describe what does hold. A causal or\npredictive model explains how an action may change the state.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":231
        },
        {
          "end_line":282,
          "quote":"Homeostasis\nmeans correction towards the required conditions as disturbances and new\nobservations arise; it guarantees neither convergence nor the adequacy of",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":280
        }
      ],
      "key":"construction_relation",
      "label":"Construction relation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"An arrangement of admissible construction and assurance serving Z within a selected resource envelope. Selection belongs to the realisation and actor exercising admitted work authority. Context limits what one activation can hold; attention limits what it can use; a frame selects one step's material and task contract while Z persists across activations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":240,
          "quote":"A strategy arranges admissible construction and assurance to\nserve Z within the selected resource envelope.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":239
        }
      ],
      "key":"strategy",
      "label":"Strategy"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The step's reconstructable governing input: governed outcome, admitted prerequisite or experiment; exact subject, basis and acquirable inputs; evaluation and result algebra; bounded affected relations and invariants; accepted transformation-admission relations; shared computational dispositions and bindings; construction, assessment and decision authorities and grant; actor capability envelopes; stale, scope and re-entry conditions; and, for a cost claim, allowance and spend measurement.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":358,
          "quote":"A step is activated from an intake sufficient to reconstruct its governing\nrelations without conversation history, commentary or a prior actor's memory\n(P0, actor-change premise). The intake names:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FIntake",
          "start_line":356
        },
        {
          "end_line":382,
          "quote":"- where the governed question is a cost claim, the allowance and how\n  spend will be measured (§6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FIntake",
          "start_line":381
        }
      ],
      "key":"intake",
      "label":"Intake"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable of delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing relation. It need not coincide with a function, file, module, ticket field or design document. It supplies the context-construction seed set Z, whose meaning differs from destination Z; context is its projection.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":405,
          "quote":"The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable\nof delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing\nrelation.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit",
          "start_line":397
        },
        {
          "end_line":405,
          "quote":"The cone is the seed set Z of §2; the context is its projection.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit",
          "start_line":405
        }
      ],
      "key":"execution_unit",
      "label":"Execution unit"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A step contract has at least drafted, admitted, rejected and superseded states. Admission is distinct from drafting and validates the exact contract against its cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis; it does not admit that basis or create or renew unadmitted authority. An admitted contract identifies a durable result and evidence surface.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":413,
          "quote":"Drafting a step's contract and admitting it are distinct relations, even\ninside one invocation that drafts, validates, admits and executes; no\nseparate turn, carrier or approval ceremony is implied by the distinction.\nA contract carries at minimum the states drafted, admitted, rejected and\nsuperseded",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FAdmission",
          "start_line":409
        }
      ],
      "key":"contract_admission",
      "label":"Contract and admission"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Evaluation of the predicate that an obligation applies to the exact subject, determined by the owning evaluation and scope declarations using sufficient basis-bound facts. True maps to satisfied; false maps to falsified with its basis-bound counterexample; a missing or ambiguous premise maps to indeterminate, or out_of_frame when a needed relation is undeclared. Exclusion is the obligation's state after falsified applicability, not a result of that obligation and not a core value. An owner-declared disjunction including non-application has its own predicate.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":488,
          "quote":"An exclusion is the state of the excluded obligation after a\n`falsified` applicability result: it is no result, the obligation's own\nevaluation is not performed and maps to no core value, and the obligation\nleaves the required coverage of a dependent conjunction under the cited\nauthority of that applicability result. An obligation whose applicability is\nunresolved stays in that required coverage.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FApplicability",
          "start_line":483
        }
      ],
      "key":"applicability",
      "label":"Applicability and exclusion"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A candidate together with step-produced facts: judgments and evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance and one construction-availability stop state. The actor's internal path is neither output nor governed work.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":507,
          "quote":"The step's output is a candidate plus its step-produced facts: judgments with\ntheir evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance, and\none stop state, a value of construction availability (§3). The actor's\ninternal path is not part of the output\nand is not governed",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FOutput",
          "start_line":503
        }
      ],
      "key":"step_output",
      "label":"Step output"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Allocation of task responsibilities and information exchanges to frames spanning the task's work; activation binds actors to frames. An active frame configuration is the part used for one evaluation or decision. Allocation derives from operations, dependencies, available actor capabilities and required assurance, without being uniquely determined. A coordinator, when delivery management is separated from bounded changes, retains the longer-term outcome. The optional executive example assigns construction to Worker/Writer, assessment to Reviewer, and next-work selection and disposition within grant to a non-mutating Executive.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":516,
          "quote":"A configuration allocates a task's responsibilities and information\nexchanges to frames; activation binds an actor to each frame (§2). It\nspans the task's work.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration",
          "start_line":512
        },
        {
          "end_line":618,
          "quote":"That profile owns its frames, their grants, limits and\nprohibitions, and its explanation; they apply where it is selected. It is\nnot the method's default.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration",
          "start_line":615
        }
      ],
      "key":"configuration",
      "label":"Configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Roles are configuration-allocated relations over steps, not actor kinds or a fixed inventory. Where present, constructor owns bounded implementation and self-review, assessor independently evaluates a frozen candidate, and decision owner disposes. A bounded proxy is a delegation whose authority relation determines whether it may accept and advance routine actions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":641,
          "quote":"Roles are relations over steps that a configuration allocates\n(Configuration above), not kinds of actor and not a fixed inventory.\nWhere a configuration's operations include construction, assessment or\ndisposition, this member names the responsibility for each: a\nconstructor owns the bounded implementation and its self-review; an\nassessor evaluates a frozen candidate independently; a decision owner\ndisposes.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation",
          "start_line":635
        }
      ],
      "key":"roles_and_proxy",
      "label":"Roles and bounded proxy"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Source-defined procedure taking seed set Z, dependency relation family R and actor envelope B: compute exact finite unique material closure, project with boundary seams, measure and test context fit when capacity is declared, then acquire exact declared inputs. R includes dependencies whose change can alter result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency or authority. Activation binds a reusable frame or active configuration to exact subject and basis and loads its declared material and evidence sources.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":713,
          "quote":"Given a seed set Z (the subject, outcome and affected relations named in the\nintake), a relation family R (the dependency relations whose change can\nalter the result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency or authority), and\nthe actor's envelope B:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":710
        }
      ],
      "key":"context_construction",
      "label":"Context construction and activation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Read-only observation of the frame, subject and declared inputs within intake permission. Acquisition is neither admission nor a further actor stage and grants no role, operation or decision.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":800,
          "quote":"Acquisition is the read-only observation of the material a\nstep needs (its frame, its subject and its declared inputs) within the\ninputs its intake permits it to acquire (§1 Intake). It is not an admission and not a further\nactor stage; effectful work still needs its admitted contract (§1\nAdmission), and acquiring material grants no role, operation or decision",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":794
        }
      ],
      "key":"acquisition",
      "label":"Acquisition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Material copied, projected or compressed from named owning sources, such as a projected frame or a task constraint surface from a current a_c interpretation. It owns no determination. Currentness is relative to every named source identity in a selected basis, and is separate from fidelity and question-specific sufficiency.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":806,
          "quote":"A derived surface is material derived from owning\nsources by copying, projection or compression, such as a projected frame\nfor a task; it names its sources and owns no determination.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":800
        },
        {
          "end_line":924,
          "quote":"Matching source identities establish only that the surface was derived\n  from those sources. They establish neither its fidelity to them nor its\n  sufficiency for a question",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope%2FStaleness%20of%20derived%20surfaces",
          "start_line":921
        }
      ],
      "key":"derived_surface",
      "label":"Derived surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A rendered contract over typed authority, projecting the material selected through acquisition; it is not source law.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":867,
          "quote":"A prompt is rendered contract over typed authority;\nit is not source law.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":864
        }
      ],
      "key":"prompt_contract",
      "label":"Prompt contract"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Each performed evaluation returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome; an unperformed evaluation has no result. Five distinct refinements answer whether a step may begin, whether a candidate is available, whether a candidate is accepted at its declared boundary, whether an ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis, and whether an intended external effect occurred.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":955,
          "quote":"each evaluation it\nperformed returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome,\nand an evaluation it did not perform has no result.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition",
          "start_line":946
        }
      ],
      "key":"step_result_algebra",
      "label":"Step results and five refinements"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"For the predicate 'the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis': activated maps to satisfied when contract admission has evidence, Z/R/required-edge semantics/basis/scope are exact, closure is finite and unique, projection supplies selected context and frame activation returns activated_frame; admission_refused(authority) maps to out_of_frame for unadmitted work authority or unavailable/unauthorised durable evidence surface and names the missing authority or surface and owner; admission_refused(basis) maps to invalid_basis when the cited outcome/prerequisite/experiment or named subject/basis cannot support the contract; closure_unresolved maps to invalid_basis for inexact closure inputs, nonfinite/nonunique closure or projection gap/refusal and names failed condition and basis coordinates; out_of_frame maps to out_of_frame for an undeclared required relation/capability in all available frame/actor pairings or no fitting context option; activation_refusal retains the cause-specific mapping owned by REFERENCE_FRAME §5.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":994,
          "quote":"| `activated` | the contract is admitted with its admission evidence (§1), Z, R, the required-edge semantics, the basis and the scope are exact and the material closure is finite and unique (§2, step 1), its projection returns a selected context (§2, step 2), and activation returns `activated_frame` | satisfied |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAdmission%20and%20activation",
          "start_line":989
        }
      ],
      "key":"admission_activation_outcome",
      "label":"Admission and activation outcomes"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["Lawful activation occurred."],
      "definition":"Availability of a constructing step's exact constructed candidate or an assessing step's closed results. For 'a candidate is available': candidate_ready → satisfied when exact candidate and transition evidence exist; refused → falsified when a governing prohibition or owner-valid construction refusal defeats construction, with that prohibition/refusal as counterexample; incomplete → falsified when the step stops without output because a needed evaluation was unperformed or undecidable on admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first, with stop basis and residuals naming which; re_entry_requested(authority) → out_of_frame for a needed decision outside grant, naming its owner; re_entry_requested(basis) → invalid_basis when activated basis no longer supports work.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1022,
          "quote":"| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability",
          "start_line":1018
        }
      ],
