      "statement":"Transitions compose only under refinement. Intake binds current state through exact subject/basis, destination or prerequisite through governed outcome, and preserved obligations through affected relations/invariants. Discovery can add obligations and enlarge known work; invalidated claims must be re-established or withdrawn before reliance. Obligations outside current attention remain open, and the next decision retains material dependencies on them. Authorised destination changes follow the owner and re-enter the owning relation; revised satisfaction proves nothing about former satisfaction. Completion requires sufficient evidence that current state satisfies applicable destination and acceptance conditions, with acceptance belonging to the decision owner; empty lists, counts and absence of recorded counterexamples do not establish it. Inability to continue causes an explicit cause-named stop: unavailable output takes non-candidate_ready availability; halting/out-of-authority ambiguity takes blocked/escalated; refused admission/activation creates no step. Stops retain outcome, residuals and debts. Progress uses outcome evidence, not remaining-item count. Intake and work state already carry the bindings; no further carrier is required.",
