      "statement":"Execute only after exact-contract admission. The drafting actor cannot infer admission from its draft, carrier, lane or active label or self-certify its execution basis. Admitted result identifies mechanism, authority, exact identity/digest, decision and evidence including override; without those coordinates the contract remains drafted or rejected, and assertion prose is not evidence. Admission validates against but does not admit the cited basis; drafting/admission/retention creates or renews no unadmitted authority. Only an admitted contract activates a step: results, child completion, tool/model output, shared actors and lateral handoffs alone neither activate another step nor authorise continuation; routing profiles name their instances of this rule. Before return record every result, withheld closure and residual obligation on the one authorised available durable surface. Conversation alone is insufficient. Missing/rejected admission returns cause-named admission_refused and missing work authority without execution. Carrier selection remains TICKETS tier-2 law.",
