      "key":"applicability_coverage_and_qualification",
      "statement":"True applicability requires the obligation's evaluation/result; false applicability excludes only that obligation under cited authority, recording inapplicability apart from its result and waiving no acceptance criterion. Missing/ambiguous premises are unresolved, never false; they retain required coverage and withhold dependent claims until evidence or owner decision resolves them. Frame names, available tools and listed families do not activate work. Residual semantic judgment and evidence remain judgment, never computed fact. Absent, stale, wrong-subject/basis or incapable required results cannot satisfy dependent conjunctions; other applicable constraints remain effective even if detected once. Under a finite declared fixture, qualification distinguishes true/false/unknown premises, missing/wrong-subject required results and sufficient positive result; always-skip/always-activate rules cannot satisfy those outcomes. Excluded obligations are unperformed and have no core value. Non-application can satisfy only an explicitly declared disjunction, never the obligation-holds predicate. Members/profiles/projects refer to this exclusion rule rather than deciding it again.",
